## What a power purchase agreement covers

Under a power purchase agreement we own the system, and you buy what it produces.

- Ampfield builds, owns and insures the system
- You pay for each kilowatt-hour it delivers
  - At a price fixed for 10 to 20 years
  - With no payment up front

:::list{markers="v"}

What is included:

- Service, repairs and insurance
- Monitoring every minute by Ampfield Pilot, with a report each month

:::

:::list{markers="x"}

What is not:

- A payment up front
- The risk that the system produces less than promised

:::

:::list{markers="1./a)"}

How the term ends:

1. You choose one of three
   1. Extend the agreement
   2. Buy the system at its value then
   3. Have it removed at our cost
2. You tell us a year before the term ends

:::

:::list{markers="1/1.1"}

1. Survey
   1. Roof
   2. Switchboard
2. Design
   1. Yield model

:::

- [x] Meter data sent
- [ ] Roof drawings found
- [ ] Date for the visit agreed

:::::`} />

